The plate spans about 390 px, which I take as roughly 26 cm, so 1 cm is about 15 px. The food is a pile of soft white curds about 100 px wide (roughly 7 cm) and 160 px long (roughly 10 cm). That is about 50–60 cm² of footprint. I estimate the height at 1.5–2 cm, so the volume is around 90 cm³. Loosely packed curds should weigh roughly 0.6 g/cm³, which gives about 55–60 g.

The curds look like scrambled egg whites, so I use 55 kcal/100 g.

